1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,271
This text looks like it's from your bank.

2
00:00:06,451 --> 00:00:08,251
It isn't.

3
00:00:08,711 --> 00:00:10,750
Let's take it apart.

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:15,724
Welcome to the safety classroom.

5
00:00:16,177 --> 00:00:19,440
Today's lesson: the fake bank text.

6
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:22,750
Five tricks. And five answers.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,124
Trick one. The bait.

8
00:00:27,917 --> 00:00:30,130
A message arrives from a bank

9
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:32,009
you may even use.

10
00:00:33,338 --> 00:00:35,079
It says there is a problem

11
00:00:35,099 --> 00:00:36,899
with your account.

12
00:00:38,197 --> 00:00:39,743
It uses the bank's name,

13
00:00:39,763 --> 00:00:41,813
and it sounds official.

14
00:00:43,143 --> 00:00:45,263
But anyone can type any name

15
00:00:45,283 --> 00:00:47,083
into a text.

16
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,195
Trick two. The panic.

17
00:00:52,049 --> 00:00:54,994
The message gives you a deadline.

18
00:00:56,410 --> 00:00:57,703
Act in ten minutes,

19
00:00:57,723 --> 00:01:00,416
or your account will be frozen.

20
00:01:01,831 --> 00:01:03,920
Real problems rarely arrive

21
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:05,817
with a countdown.

22
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:08,427
The clock is there

23
00:01:08,447 --> 00:01:10,750
to stop you from thinking.

24
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,197
Trick three. The link.

25
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:18,012
To fix everything,

26
00:01:18,032 --> 00:01:20,719
you only have to tap one link.

27
00:01:23,113 --> 00:01:25,381
Look closely. The address is close

28
00:01:25,401 --> 00:01:28,441
to the real one, but not quite right.

29
00:01:30,835 --> 00:01:32,956
One small change in one word

30
00:01:32,976 --> 00:01:34,776
is all it takes.

31
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,495
Trick four. The copycat.

32
00:01:40,713 --> 00:01:42,329
The page behind the link

33
00:01:42,349 --> 00:01:44,671
looks just like your bank.

34
00:01:46,242 --> 00:01:49,067
Same colors. Same logo.

35
00:01:50,639 --> 00:01:53,285
But it is only a costume.

36
00:01:55,210 --> 00:01:56,750
Everything you type goes

37
00:01:56,770 --> 00:01:58,750
straight to the thief.

38
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,273
Trick five. The code.

39
00:02:03,872 --> 00:02:05,971
Now the thief tries to log in

40
00:02:05,991 --> 00:02:08,075
to your real account.

41
00:02:08,904 --> 00:02:12,266
Your bank sends you a one-time code.

42
00:02:13,094 --> 00:02:14,957
The thief asks you for it,

43
00:02:14,977 --> 00:02:17,264
by text or on the phone.

44
00:02:18,093 --> 00:02:19,574
That code is a key.

45
00:02:19,594 --> 00:02:22,750
Hand it over, and the door opens.

46
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,200
Let's go back.

47
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,165
Answer one. Pause.

48
00:02:33,724 --> 00:02:35,576
A message that rushes you

49
00:02:35,596 --> 00:02:37,495
is a warning sign.

50
00:02:39,405 --> 00:02:40,748
Put the phone down.

51
00:02:40,768 --> 00:02:42,824
Take one slow breath.

52
00:02:44,734 --> 00:02:46,331
Nothing real disappears

53
00:02:46,351 --> 00:02:49,150
in the time it takes to breathe.

54
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:54,014
Answer two. Don't tap.

55
00:02:55,529 --> 00:02:58,346
Ignore the link in the message.

56
00:03:00,204 --> 00:03:02,107
Open your bank's app yourself,

57
00:03:02,127 --> 00:03:04,535
or type the address you know.

58
00:03:06,394 --> 00:03:08,087
If there is a real problem,

59
00:03:08,107 --> 00:03:10,750
it will be waiting for you there.

60
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:16,330
Answer three. Keep the code.

61
00:03:17,529 --> 00:03:20,725
A one-time code is for you alone.

62
00:03:22,216 --> 00:03:25,182
Your bank will never ask you to read it out.

63
00:03:25,202 --> 00:03:27,721
Not in a text. Not on a call.

64
00:03:29,211 --> 00:03:32,350
If someone asks, that is the scam.

65
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:37,065
Answer four. Call back.

66
00:03:38,917 --> 00:03:41,590
If you are unsure, hang up.

67
00:03:43,843 --> 00:03:45,201
Then call the number

68
00:03:45,221 --> 00:03:47,217
printed on your card.

69
00:03:49,470 --> 00:03:51,292
Not the number in the message.

70
00:03:51,312 --> 00:03:53,950
Not the number a caller gives you.

71
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:59,036
Answer five. Lock the door.

72
00:04:00,484 --> 00:04:03,459
Turn on alerts for every payment.

73
00:04:05,241 --> 00:04:07,214
Use your bank's app sign-in,

74
00:04:07,234 --> 00:04:09,991
or a passkey, if it offers one.

75
00:04:11,772 --> 00:04:13,443
Then a stolen password

76
00:04:13,463 --> 00:04:15,550
alone is not enough.

77
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:19,612
Already tapped? Don't panic.

78
00:04:19,632 --> 00:04:22,182
It happens to careful people.

79
00:04:23,074 --> 00:04:24,413
One. Call your bank,

80
00:04:24,433 --> 00:04:27,021
using the number on your card.

81
00:04:27,553 --> 00:04:29,771
Two. Change the password you used,

82
00:04:29,791 --> 00:04:31,855
everywhere you used it.

83
00:04:32,387 --> 00:04:35,264
Three. Turn on two-step sign-in.

84
00:04:35,796 --> 00:04:37,535
Four. Check your statements,

85
00:04:37,555 --> 00:04:39,550
and report the message.

86
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,400
Remember.

87
00:04:45,414 --> 00:04:47,738
Pause. Don't tap. Keep the code.

88
00:04:47,758 --> 00:04:50,139
Call back. Lock the door.

89
00:04:52,989 --> 00:04:54,766
And share this with someone

90
00:04:54,786 --> 00:04:56,586
you care about.
